      "side": 1,
      "message": "I had missed this before, and didn\u0027t notice until I was adding the matrix multiply, but Skia\u0027s 2D -\u003e 3D model is that a local position is always (x,y,0,1). The only way to get a non-zero Z value, or a non-1 W value is if the transform matrix modifies those. This lets use reason about draws with the same transform in 2D instead of always needing Z and W as well.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 91,
        "startChar": 66,
        "endLine": 91,
        "endChar": 70
      },
      "revId": "e3583ae73e3c4a9c0ae21931ada40210dc87a342",
